    <string name="nuit_etoilee_title">The Starry Night</string>
    <string name="nuit_etoilee_note">Painted from his room at the Saint-Rémy-de-Provence asylum, just before sunrise. The village, though, is imagined.</string>
    <string name="champ_de_ble_cypres_title">Wheat Field with Cypresses</string>
    <string name="champ_de_ble_cypres_note">Van Gogh saw in cypresses “the equivalent of an Egyptian obelisk”. He painted three versions of this landscape.</string>
    <string name="cafe_de_nuit_title">The Night Café</string>
    <string name="cafe_de_nuit_note">“I have tried to express the terrible passions of humanity by means of red and green,” he wrote to his brother Theo.</string>
    <string name="maisons_personnage_title">Cottages and Figure</string>
    <string name="maisons_personnage_note">A memory of the North painted in Saint-Rémy: thatched cottages, curling smoke and a setting sun.</string>
    <string name="grande_vague_title">The Great Wave off Kanagawa</string>
    <string name="grande_vague_year">c. 1831</string>
    <string name="grande_vague_note">A print from the Thirty-six Views of Mount Fuji. Prussian blue, then new in Japan, makes a thunderous entrance.</string>
    <string name="naufrage_minotaure_title">The Wreck of a Transport Ship</string>
    <string name="naufrage_minotaure_year">c. 1810</string>
    <string name="naufrage_minotaure_note">Turner, painter of light and storms, heralds the Impressionists here by more than half a century.</string>
    <string name="le_cri_title">The Scream</string>
    <string name="le_cri_note">“I sensed an infinite scream passing through nature.” The red sky may be a sunset over Oslo.</string>
